From: nuubOS <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: EGL config for GLES2 contexts in GLES3 builds

A build with --enable-opengles3 defines HAVE_OPENGLES3 but not
HAVE_OPENGLES2, so the Wayland context selected no EGL config attributes
when the gl driver asks for a GLES 2 context and egl_init_context()
dereferenced a NULL attribute list (SIGSEGV at startup). Use the ES2
renderable-type attributes for every GLES context below version 3.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/gfx/drivers_context/wayland_ctx.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers_context/wayland_ctx.c
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@
    };
 
 #ifdef HAVE_OPENGLES
-#ifdef HAVE_OPENGLES2
+#if defined(HAVE_OPENGLES2) || defined(HAVE_OPENGLES3)
    static const EGLint egl_attribs_gles[] = {
       WL_EGL_ATTRIBS_BASE,
       EGL_RENDERABLE_TYPE, EGL_OPENGL_ES2_BIT,
@@ -221,10 +221,8 @@
          else
 #endif
 #endif
-#ifdef HAVE_OPENGLES2
             attrib_ptr = egl_attribs_gles;
 #endif
-#endif
          break;
       case GFX_CTX_OPENVG_API:
 #ifdef HAVE_VG
